# Diagnosis: make discovered fitting obstacles inspectable

The original twenty-game baseline report is
5ea2ba333bf885c7fea32ec5b8cb27223639ec5a7641dae81b4e33c37a242551.
Source row 8 reaches two of eight selected player-specific milestones in
2,540 nodes and then reports an unsupported boundary. Its receipt retains a
prefix and a generic explanation, but does not show which original transition
prevented the observation check. The eight matching games likewise lack
recorded field-by-field engine values for the viewer.

This is a diagnosis of the measurement and explanation machinery. It does
not establish an MTG rules error. The candidate adds typed traces of the
original submitted actions, events and projected states, plus source-field
comparisons and a separately identified failing branch.

The unsupported projection messages also need more precise explanations.
The independent source diagnosis artifact
6efc5660277c276eb704087d2b8e64aaa0566b0e15f350b1e8ec7b25751fa014
preserves twelve negative combat-damage observations from the exact full
source rows. Neither the inspected official schema helper nor client source
established that this column equals native combat damage events. The native
mana expenditure events also do not cover every payment path. Ability IDs
require their own binding. Consequently all these observations remain
unsupported; a diagnostic native combat total is explicitly unchecked.

The change preserves legal action search, boundary guards, reconstruction,
enforced observations, Phase revision and existing issue identities. It
improves source reasons and stores a diagnostic code/reason in issue
evidence while retaining the earlier grouping detail for compatibility.

The independent static trace review pins the six native source files.
Tests replay successful and failed paths through the production engine and
check original event/state equality, branch separation and lack of invented
actual values for unsupported, unknown or unreached fields. The locked
workspace tests and required Rust checks passed.

The exact patch is against the baseline worker's source commit. That commit
preceded the already-published measurement documentation; the full commit
diff therefore also retains those documentation changes. The substantive
native trace changes are the six reviewed bridge/fitter files.

The same twenty cases will run with the same manifest, node/action bounds
and sixty-second external deadline. The intended improvement is inspectable
evidence. This proposal does not promise fewer unsupported cases, treat
changed wording as an issue resolution, or authorize an acceptance decision.
